I used INLA on Rstudio desktop without (many) problems but now my organisation has switched to RStudio server<div><br></div><div>When I now try to install INLA using</div><div><br></div><div>install.packages(&quot;INLA&quot;,repos=c(getOption(&quot;repos&quot;),INLA=&quot;<a href="https://inla.r-inla-download.org/R/stable" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://inla.r-inla-download.org/R/stable&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792439695257000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0sYcNlpRHHbZ76w3qAt_tN">https://inla.r-inla-download.org/R/stable</a>&quot;), dep=TRUE)<br></div><div><br></div><div>I get </div><div>&quot;Warning in install.packages :
  package ‘INLA’ is not available for this version of R&quot;<br></div><div>When I use R 4.0.3</div><div>&quot;Warning in install.packages :
  package ‘INLA’ is not available (for R version 3.6.3)&quot; and </div><div>&quot;Warning in install.packages :
  package ‘INLA’ is not available (for R version 3.6.0)&quot;</div><div><br></div><div>Are these error messages correct? </div><div><br></div><div>Martin</div><div><br></div>
